{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"199571e90ec1e7271dce85fd6ac644b86761156a64c93af7114db57106564fed","digest":{"component_or_area":"backtest planning corpus analysis","key_entities":["scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py","PLANNING_CORPUS_SIZE","PLANNING_CORPUS_COMMITS","PLANNING_CORPUS_BOUNDARY","--check-planning-corpus","ADJUDICATED_SUBSTANTIVE","_resolve_bug_ticket","ticket_type"],"problem_keywords":["planning corpus","corpus pin","commit identity","drift","backtest"],"propositions":["The corpus size constant (113) is asserted against a live re-derivation that changes when tickets are reclassified or prefix resolution shifts, causing the check to fail on main with corpus=114.","Pinning by count is fragile; the corpus must be pinned by commit identity (frozenset of 113 SHAs) so the check is immune to tracker churn and historical ticket metadata changes.","The --check-planning-corpus script mode should iterate the pinned SHA set directly and measure each, validating identity and flagged set equality rather than re-deriving membership from live state.","Per-row ticket labels should remain best-effort artifact metadata and never gate the check's pass/fail logic."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787764478946303001,"uuid":"d97430d0-0f11-467c-93eb-7b69d68d7b28"}